desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Hooks Wget Pipe Bash Generic"
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Wget Pipe Bash Generic",
	type: vuln
	level: critical
	rule_id: "source-config-hooks-wget-pipe-bash-generic"
	risk: "security-misconfiguration"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `hooks-wget-pipe-bash-generic` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/hooks-wget-pipe-bash/hooks-wget-pipe-bash.yaml).
Original message: Remote script is fetched and piped directly to a shell interpreter. In Claude Code and Cursor hooks, this enables remote code execution from untrusted sources. Download the script first, inspect it, then execute it separately.

CWE: CWE-829: Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere
References:
- https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks
- https://cursor.com/docs/agent/hooks
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sh": <<<POS
wget
W67+SQc|zsh

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.sh}.pattern_regex(/(curl|wget)\s+.*\|\s*(bash|sh|zsh)\b/) as $p0
${*.bash}.pattern_regex(/(curl|wget)\s+.*\|\s*(bash|sh|zsh)\b/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "Hooks Wget Pipe Bash Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Wget Pipe Bash Generic",
	message: "Hooks Wget Pipe Bash Generic",
}
